
# live-pipeline
- label: run↔session attribution is spawn-identity-first (src/sessions/run-session-link.js): POST /api/runs generates a session UUID for agents whose CLI accepts one (agentSupportsSessionId — exactly claude and grok, verified against their --help; buildLaunchArgv places --session-id <uuid> BEFORE the end-of-options "--" prompt marker, agents without the flag get no uuid) and persists it as the run window's tq_session_id tmux user option, so the agent NAMES its recording after the uuid (<uuid>.jsonl under .claude/projects/<slug-of-cwd>, the <uuid>/ session dir under .grok/sessions/<enc-cwd>) and attribution is deterministic BEFORE the first byte is written — no fd evidence needed (the real claude CLI appends open/write/close and NEVER holds its recording open, so fd-probing can never fire for it); expectedSessionPaths/spawnIdentitySessionPath compute the determined path set for BOTH cwd spellings (literal + realpath), and every agent with a session-id launch flag has a computable expected-path layout
  id: clsi
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'spawn identity|session-id|session uuid|spawn-time|FRESH uuid' test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js test/agents/agent-detect.test.js test/routes/launch-routes.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: a spawn-identified run (tq_session_id set) can NEVER mislink — it links exactly the recording named by its uuid the moment that recording exists and NOTHING ELSE ever (pending until then, even when other candidate recordings sit in the same cwd), a stale pre-upgrade heuristic claim on such a run is dropped AND cleared from tmux on the first poll instead of being served (even on an exited run), and non-identified runs can never steal an identified run's determined recording — expectedSessionPaths of every other identified window are excluded from their candidate sets even before the identified run links, while identified rivals no longer CONTEST other runs' own uncontested candidates (their claim is settled by construction)
  id: clnm
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'spawn identity' test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: src/sessions/run-session-link.js attributes a Run to the session recording its agent process writes, identity-first with heuristics last — tier 0 spawn identity (the determined tq_session_id recording, see clsi/clnm), then for runs WITHOUT spawn identity, candidates from the launched agent's own session root under $HOME in the agent's REAL on-disk layout, built by the SHARED layout module fact cllay names (claude: .claude/projects/<DASH-slug of cwd>/*.jsonl for BOTH the literal tq_cwd and its realpath spellings; cursor-agent: .cursor/projects/<DASHLESS slug>/agent-transcripts/<uuid>/<uuid>.jsonl, main recordings only — subagent transcripts are a session's children, never a run's own recording; codex: rollout-*.jsonl in the dated .codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD tree; droid: <ws-dir>/*.jsonl one level under .factory/sessions; grok: session DIRECTORIES under .grok/sessions/<enc-cwd> timed and probed via chat_history.jsonl), only recordings CREATED (birthtime, mtime fallback) at/after the run's tq_started minus a 2s slack qualify (the user's own pre-existing session in the same cwd is filtered out), paths identity-claimed by other runs (persisted pid/sid/prompt links, EXITED runs' final claims of any attr, every identified run's expected paths, and every DISMISSED run's tombstoned claim — fact cltb) are excluded, and attributeRunSession classifies every candidate by identity evidence — a file held open by THIS run's pane process tree (tmux pane_pid expanded via descendantPids, holders via the pid-keyed openPathHolders probe) is pid-CONFIRMED, one held open by a rival run's tree OR whose first user message matches a rival's persisted prompt (fact clpc) is FOREIGN and can never link here, and an unvouched file is only a heuristic guess while NO rival (living window, or pending-at-death tombstone) whose ownable window admits it also claims it AND it is the SOLE eligible candidate (two unvouched recordings born after the run start are indistinguishable — birth order and anonymous fd holders select nothing; fact clha) — contested files need pid or prompt-corroboration evidence; agents without a followable per-run file recording answer no candidates so their runs stay pending — gemini writes none at all, and opencode's rows live in ONE shared SQLite file that has no per-session birth time and whose single fd is held for every session at once, so birth-gating and pid-confirmation would both fire for unrelated sessions (a RESUMED opencode run can still link its source via the fact-clrs fallback)
  id: cllk
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: a run↔session link is persisted in the run window's tq_session + tq_session_attr tmux user options via linkRunSession with a four-tier contract — attr "sid" (spawn identity: the run's own tq_session_id named the recording) and attr "pid" (pid-confirmed identity) are sticky forever, winning every poll and serve restart without re-resolution; attr "prompt" (content identity: the recording's first user message IS this run's persisted tq_prompt and no other party's) is served, settled for rivalry purposes (bars the path from other runs, stops contesting), and RE-VALIDATED every poll while the run lives — dropped to pending when a same-prompt rival whose gate admits the file makes content identity ambiguous, final on an exited run; attr "heur" (a guess — the sole eligible candidate, a unique prompt match under a coarse stone, or a resumed run's fresh source recording) is served but RE-VALIDATED on every poll — upgraded to pid/prompt when stronger evidence appears, dropped (cleared from tmux) the moment it turns out foreign, claimed, or contested, DEMOTED to pending the moment a second eligible candidate exists, and final on an exited run only when it was unambiguous at death (fact clha); nothing is persisted while pending, a failed persist still answers the link, and a link that would bind another run's recording is never persisted — tmux stays the only run table; src/mux/tmux.js exports setWindowOption plus setSessionOption/getSessionOption for session-scoped state, RUN_OPTION_NAMES includes tq_session_id + tq_ended + tq_resumed_path + tq_fork_prompt, and listWindows reports pane_pid + tq_session_attr + tq_session_id + tq_ended in its space-safe format and tq_session/tq_prompt/tq_resumed_path/tq_fork_prompt through id-keyed queries whose arbitrary-content value is placed last (locale-proof like window_name)
  id: clpr
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'linkRunSession|spawn identity|run session link survives a serve restart' test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js && grep -q tq_session_id src/mux/tmux.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: GET /api/runs/session?id=<runId> (registered in ROUTE_MAP, never route-cached) answers the run's LIVE unified session as JSON {run, state, link, attribution, sessionPath, etag, session, chapters}: run is the same {id, agent, cwd, startedAt, status} shape as GET /api/runs; link is pending|linked; attribution is sid (spawn identity: the launcher-generated session uuid named the recording — deterministic, sticky) or pid (identity: the recording is held open by this run's own process tree) or prompt (content identity: the recording's first user message is this run's persisted launch prompt and no other run's — dead or alive; re-validated every poll) or heuristic (uncontested birth-time match, re-validated every poll) or null while pending; state is the combined lifecycle pending|live|idle|exited (live only while generating — never merely because sessionPath exists; a linked idle TUI is idle); session/chapters are tracequest's unified representation — the parsed Session (events/stats via parseSession) of the recording the agent process itself writes, plus buildSessionChapters chapters; a malformed id answers 400, an id naming no run window answers 404, and a linked recording vanishing mid-request degrades to the pending shape rather than a 500
  id: clep
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'run session' test/routes/launch-routes.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: watching a run through /api/runs/session is LIVE and incremental: every poll re-links and re-stats the recording so events the agent appends appear in the next poll (integration: a stub agent writing claude-format JSONL grows 2→4 events, a second chapter opens, the mtimeMs-size etag moves); a request repeating the current etag answers {unchanged:true} with no session body, and the parse itself is memoized per path behind the etag so ~1s polls of an idle run cost one stat, never a reparse
  id: clfr
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'run session serves the growing unified session' test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: run+session lifecycle is fully observable for the chat UI: GET /api/runs lists every run with sessionPath/link/attribution/state alongside the existing fields (state is pending|live|idle|exited — live only while generating), a run whose agent has not (or never will have) written a recording answers the pending shape (200, link pending, null session — never an error), a linked idle TUI answers state idle, an exited run's session stays served with state exited and the full final conversation, and a serve restarted mid-run answers the same linked session immediately from persisted tmux state
  id: clst
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'run session of an exited run stays served|run session rejects malformed and unknown ids and answers pending|run session link survives a serve restart|GET /api/runs stays a plain GET route' test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js test/routes/launch-routes.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: run↔session attribution can never bind another agent's — or the user's — transcript to a run, even for agents that NEVER hold their recording open (the real claude behavior, and the round-2 failure mode): the integration stubs model it faithfully (recordings named by the spawn-assigned --session-id uuid, written open/append/close, lsof verifies ZERO holders at link time), and end-to-end against a real serve + tmux (a) two concurrent non-holding runs in ONE cwd with a sub-2s stagger BOTH link their own uuid recording as attribution sid — at no poll does either answer the other's transcript, and neither deadlocks pending-forever; (b) a user's own session file born after a run's start in the same cwd is NEVER served for that run — the run honestly pends until ITS uuid recording appears, then links it; (c) a poisoned pre-upgrade heuristic claim (the user's session persisted as tq_session attr heur) is dropped and CLEARED on the first poll after a serve restart instead of being served forever; the persisted tmux state carries attr sid so the correct links survive restarts
  id: clid
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'pid attribution|NON-HOLDING|NEVER served|poisoned pre-upgrade|spawn identity' test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: run↔session attribution has a CONTENT-identity tier for the five registry agents WITHOUT a --session-id mechanism (codex, cursor-agent, opencode, droid, gemini): every prompted launch persists its prompt in the tq_prompt window option (activitySnippet single line), the linker extracts a candidate recording's FIRST user message (peekSession in the agent's own dialect, memoized per path — immutable once non-null), and promptCorroborates compares them (whitespace-collapsed; clipped 140-char prompts match by prefix, unclipped EXACTLY) so that (a) a candidate whose first message matches a DIFFERENT run's prompt — live, exited, or tombstoned, gated by that party's ownable time window — is FOREIGN and can never link here, (b) a candidate matching THIS run's prompt and nobody else's is CORROBORATED and links even while contested (attr prompt) — two prompted non-identity runs in ONE cwd disambiguate and serve their own transcripts while BOTH live, (c) identical prompts prove nothing: both runs stay pending (pending beats wrong), (d) self-recognition: a prompted run never links a recording whose known first message mismatches its own prompt, even uncontested with no rival in sight (the launder is refused even without a tombstone), (e) a rival whose prompt provably mismatches a recording's first message cannot contest it, so a bare run's own file stays linkable next to a prompted rival, and (f) a RESUMED run's follow-up tq_prompt is never content identity in either direction — a fork recording opens with the SOURCE conversation, not the follow-up prompt, so contentPromptOf substitutes tq_fork_prompt (fact clrs) and the follow-up never disowns or fakes ambiguity against anyone
  id: clpc
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'prompt corroboration|prompt corroborates|two live prompted|identical prompts|mismatches its own prompt|NO user message|bare run|CAN.T own|disambiguates' test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: a dismissed run's claim on its recording OUTLIVES its tmux window (the r3 kill-launder fix): POST /api/runs/kill records a tombstone via recordRunTombstone BEFORE kill-window — {id, agent, cwd, started, killed, prompt, sessionId, session, attr} appended to the tq_tombstones SESSION-level tmux user option (base64 UTF-8 JSON: locale-proof ASCII, never tmux-format-expandable; RELEVANCE-capped at TOMBSTONE_MAX=32 — fact clrv — same-window entries replaced) — and readRunTombstones feeds every linkRunSession call (route handlers read once per request), so: a tombstone's claimed session path is excluded from every survivor's candidate set WHATEVER its attr, a tombstone that died PENDING keeps CONTESTING candidates born within its lifetime [started−2s, killed+2s] and keeps marking prompt-matching candidates foreign, while a tombstone that died WITH a claim bars only that path (a dead run never re-links, so it could never have owned anything else — no contested-forever), later-born files are never contested (a dead process writes nothing), a tombstone whose window still lives is ignored, garbage/absent state degrades to [], and tombstones survive serve restarts because they live in tmux — the end-to-end r3 scenario (slow-alpha survivor + killed fast-beta rival, prompted or bare) shows the survivor NEVER serving the dismissed run's transcript, before or after a restart, and linking its OWN recording when it appears
  id: cltb
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'tombstone|kill-launder|BARE survivor|kill tombstones|failed tombstone' test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js test/routes/launch-routes.test.js test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: tombstone RETENTION is by relevance, never recency (compactTombstones — the r4 contest-memory fix): a routine-dismissal flood can never evict the stone keeping an older contest honest — a stone is dropped ONLY when provably inert (no unsettled run window of its agent+cwd rivalry space — pending, heur- or prompt-linked, live or dead-pending; sid/pid links and dead runs' final claims are settled — has a candidate gate overlapping the stone's lifetime plus slack), same-space claimless stones with the same prompt MERGE into one interval-union entry (absorbed window ids remembered in ids[] so the ledger never double-tombstones them), and cap overflow FOLDS the oldest-killed stones into a COARSE per-space stone (interval-only, prompt unknown) instead of forgetting them — a coarse stone CONTESTS every candidate born inside its window and DEGRADES prompt corroboration there to guess-grade (the r5 secondary fix: a candidate whose first message uniquely matches THIS run's prompt and no known rival's SERVES under a promptUnknown owner, but only as re-validated attr heur, never settled attr prompt — an equal-prompt collider, e.g. a laundering run's own recording appearing with the same first message, demotes it again, and a bare candidate with no content match stays fully contested), while stones whose prompt matches a live unsettled run's content prompt are NEVER folded to coarse (fold the same-prompt twin's stone away and its recording would soft-corroborate as the survivor's own — same-prompt floods MERGE, so protection cannot blow the cap), so laundering stays non-final at any flood size; stones whose window still lives are kept verbatim and never merged; without a window list compaction degrades to the plain newest-N cap; end-to-end, 40 pure-API create+kill dismissal cycles after an identically-prompted twin's dismissal leave the survivor honest-pending at every poll — never serving the twin's transcript, before or after the flood — while its own late-born recording still links attr prompt
  id: clrv
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'r4 regression|routine same-space dismissals|COARSE stone|no unsettled run|window still LIVES|r4 vector 1' test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: a run window that vanishes WITHOUT passing through POST /api/runs/kill (tmux kill-window / the default prefix-& binding / kill-session — even while serve is DOWN) still leaves a tombstone: run polls (GET /api/runs, GET /api/runs/session, and run resolution inside /api/sessions/live) reconcile the tq_run_ledger SESSION-level tmux option (base64 JSON of every live run window's id/agent/cwd/started/content-prompt/sessionId/claim+attr, written by syncRunLedger only when it changed, entered at run creation so a kill before the first poll is covered too, resumed runs ledgered with a BLANK content prompt) against the actual window list — a ledger entry whose window is GONE and whose id no tombstone answers for (merged ids[] included) gets a SYNTHESIZED tombstone carrying its last-known claim, prompt and lifetime with killed = the entry's stamped exit boundary (ended, for windows that died before vanishing) or detection time (at/after the real death, so the contested window only widens: pending beats wrong); API-killed runs are never double-tombstoned, the ledger survives serve restarts (tmux stays the only run table), and callers that stub the tmux layer must opt in via deps.syncRunLedger (stubbed windows are never synced into a real tmux server); end-to-end: a bare survivor NEVER serves a tmux-killed rival's transcript — the dead run's recording sits unserved beside the survivor's own — even when the kill-window happens while serve is stopped and the diff is only seen after a restart
  id: cllg
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'run ledger|ledgered|synthesized|reconcile the ledger|r4 vector 2' test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js test/routes/launch-routes.test.js test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js && grep -q tq_run_ledger src/sessions/run-session-link.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: prompt equality is corroboration, NOT identity (the r4 equal-prompt collision fix) — when the SAME first user message exists in two or more candidate recordings (e.g. the user's own session opens with the exact text the run was launched with), content identity selects nothing — attributeRunSession refuses to corroborate ANY collider, none of them may be served as a heuristic guess either, a persisted attr-prompt claim on one collider is dropped AND cleared from tmux the moment the second appears (the wrong transcript is never kept after the run's real recording lands), and the run stays honest-pending until another tier disambiguates (pid identity picks the recording the run's own tree holds) or a collider disappears (unique corroboration returns and the run links its own recording attr prompt)
  id: clqc
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'equal-prompt|r4 vector 3' test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: the heuristic tier obeys the equal-prompt rule (the r5 promptless-mislink fix) — a guess needs a SOLE eligible candidate and dies with ambiguity, across the whole lifecycle: (a) selection — attributeRunSession answers no heuristic when two or more unvouched candidates survive the gate (birth order and anonymous fd holders are not identity), so a promptless run beside ANY concurrent same-space recording (incl. codex/droid machine-wide dated-tree spaces) stays honest-pending; (b) demotion — a persisted attr-heur guess is dropped AND cleared from tmux the moment a second eligible candidate exists (the user's session guessed during agent startup is demoted the moment the run's OWN recording lands — the wrong transcript is never kept), and relinks only when the candidate space collapses back to one (a collider claimed elsewhere, turned foreign, or gone); (c) exit boundary — the first poll that observes a run's death stamps tq_ended (detection time, at/after the real death; frozen once stamped, persisted in tmux), a dead run's candidate space is bounded to [tq_started−2s, tq_ended+2s], a guess that was UNIQUE for that whole window is the final answer forever (a later-born candidate can neither link nor demote it), and a guess that was AMBIGUOUS inside it is never finalized — cleared and pending, even when the ambiguity is first seen after the exit or across a serve restart; end-to-end (real serve + tmux + non-holding cursor-agent stub): promptless run + user session written in-cwd during startup → the sole-candidate guess serves transiently, is demoted to pending when the run's own recording appears, stays pending at every subsequent poll, and the exited run remains pending — the user's private chat is never the final answer; a BARE guess additionally serves a probation before it is served or finalized at all (fact clgp)
  id: clha
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'r5 vector|r5 regression|ambiguity rule|AMBIGUOUS at death|exit boundary|unambiguous at death|promptless codex' test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: a RESUMED run (tq_resumed_from set) never links by bare birth-time guessing — its recording is, by construction, either a FORK opening with the source conversation or the SOURCE recording itself, so an unrelated fresh file can never honestly be its transcript (attributeRunSession guessAllowed=false); instead it links through (a) spawn identity where the agent supports it (claude/grok fork uuids, unchanged), (b) CONTENT identity against tq_fork_prompt — POST /api/runs resume mode peeks the source session's first user message (peekSession, same activitySnippet clipping as tq_prompt) and persists it, so the linker recognizes the fork recording (attr prompt when the match is unique; equal-prompt collision rules apply — two forks of one source stay pending until pid evidence; the fork prompt also travels through tombstones and the ledger as the resumed run's content prompt), and (c) the SOURCE fallback — tq_resumed_path (the resolved source recording path, persisted at resume time) links as a re-validated guess (attr heur) once its freshness file's mtime moves at/after the run start and, for dead runs, within [started−2s, ended+2s] — serving the very conversation the run resumes can never be the wrong transcript, a dead resumed run's established source claim is final, and an idle source proves nothing (pending); a resumed run with neither fork-prompt nor source evidence stays honestly pending rather than guessing
  id: clrs
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'RESUMED run|resumed run|resume mode persists' test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js test/routes/launch-routes.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: GET /api/sessions/live never mislabels a recording's source — when the session-list entry is missing (a recording created seconds ago that discovery has not indexed) or carries no source, the body's source is derived from the recording PATH (sourceForSessionPath — .cursor→cursor, .codex→codex, .factory→factory, .grok→grok, opencode://→opencode, the cursor-cloud import root→cursor-cloud, claude only as the family fallback) and the SAME source is handed to the parser, so a .cursor/projects recording is never labeled or parsed as "claude"; POST /api/runs RESUME mode uses the same fallback (createResumedRun: sessions.find(...)?.source ?? sourceForSessionPath(path)) instead of defaulting unindexed paths to claude, so continuing a freshly written .cursor recording picks cursor-agent's resume mechanism and parses the source in its own dialect
  id: clsc
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'source correctness|path-derived source|UNINDEXED recording' test/routes/session-live-routes.test.js test/routes/launch-routes.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: every agent's on-disk recording LAYOUT is defined exactly once, in src/sessions/session-layout.js, and all three consumers build their paths from it — discovery (session-discovery.js: roots, the cursor agent-transcripts/<uuid>/<uuid>.jsonl nesting, the codex rollout-* predicate, the grok chat file), live detection (live-sessions.js: claude project dir, cursor transcripts dir, factory workspace dir, grok session dir; cursorProjectSlug/factoryWorkspaceSlug re-exported for callers) run attribution (run-session-link.js: runSessionCandidates + expectedSessionPaths + sessionFreshnessPath) and the live-reload data watcher (server-live-reload.js defaultDataRoots, which had been missing the cursor projects root entirely, so appends to a live cursor recording ticked nothing) — so the halves of tracequest can never disagree about where an agent writes: the round-6 defect was attribution scanning ~/.cursor/projects/<LEADING-DASH slug>/*.jsonl, a layout the real Cursor CLI has never used (verified on a real machine: 917 recordings, ALL at <dashless>/agent-transcripts/<uuid>/<uuid>.jsonl, ZERO at project-dir root), while findCursorSessions already modelled the real one — every fresh cursor-agent run pended forever with its transcript on disk; a cross-module parity test seeds one REAL recording per source under a temp HOME and asserts each per-source candidate scan finds exactly the path discovery indexes, and the attribution stubs in test/bin + test/helpers write the REAL per-source layouts and line shapes (cursor uuid-nested {"role":...} transcripts, claude dash-slug {"type":...} recordings) so a layout regression fails a test instead of passing five rounds unnoticed
  id: cllay
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'REAL CLI layout|candidate scan finds|workspace-root recordings|ignore non-rollout|canonical session roots' test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js test/sessions/discovery-paths-consistency.test.js test/server/server-live-reload.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: a BARE guess (a sole eligible candidate with NO affirmative evidence — no fd holder in this run's tree, no prompt corroboration, not a resumed run's own source) must serve a PROBATION of GUESS_PROBATION_MS = 3000 measured from the candidate's BIRTH before it is served or finalized: while the run lives the guess links only once born+probation <= now (so a foreign file that is briefly the only candidate during agent startup is not served on the first poll — the r6 transient shrinks from "wrong until the run's own recording lands" to a bounded window), and for a DEAD run the clock stops at the tq_ended exit boundary, so finalizing at death requires either an affirmative tier (sid/pid/prompt, or a resumed run's source claim) or a guess that matured WHILE THE RUN RAN — a promptless run that crashes before writing anything therefore ends "pending" forever instead of permanently binding the user's session born in its window (zero-evidence attribution), while a run that lived with its uncontested recording present for >= 3s still finalizes it; the window is birth-based, not observation-based, so the verdict is identical across polls, serve restarts and serve downtime, and the honest cost is that a promptless non-identity run's first link lands ~3s later than before (spawn-identity, pid, prompt-corroborated, unique-soft-match and resumed-source links are untouched and still land on the first poll that sees their evidence)
  id: clgp
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'probation|crashes before writing|DID mature' test/sessions/run-session-link.test.js test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: codex injects its instruction context into the FIRST user response_item as plain input_text; most blocks are XML-wrapped and fall to the "<" hidden-block rule, but the AGENTS.md injection is markdown ("# AGENTS.md instructions for <path>") and was therefore read as user speech — isCodexDisplayableUserText (src/parse/codex-event-msg.js) now excludes it, and sidecar/src/indexer.rs mirrors the same predicate for both the response_item and event_msg user_message paths so the JS parser and the Rust indexer agree on first_prompt and indexed terms; verified against 757 real rollouts on a live machine (725 carried the injection, every one starting with that exact prefix, the true prompt always arriving later as its own user item plus a verbatim event_msg user_message), and the consequences of getting it wrong were user-visible everywhere the first user message is used: session titles and search text showed the injection instead of the prompt, and run attribution could never link a prompted codex run because prompt corroboration compared the launch prompt against the injection and skipped the run own rollout forever
  id: clcx
